{
  "version": 2,
  "notes": "A vacancy in a Chern insulator (embedding)\nSpinless electrons on the honeycomb lattice with the Haldane coupling, a Chern insulator (s1), and the same system with a vacancy, a large onsite energy on one site (s2), embedded in it (e1): the vacancy sits in the infinite crystal, without the images of a supercell. The DOS of the defect's cell (c1) has a peak at zero energy, inside the gap, that the pristine cell does not have: a state bound to the vacancy. Its map (c2) sits on the three neighbours of the vacancy and decays into the bulk, and c3 gives its energy and the gap. Add a sublattice imbalance to both systems and the bound state moves away from zero (to about -0.1 for a mass of 0.2).",
